  "id": "COMPOUND:17163 - PROTEIN:5792",
  "verbalization": "Norarecoline is implicated in the relationship with RWLeu4 through a series of molecular interactions involving dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family members. The evidence suggests that Norarecoline acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol, (2E,4E)-N-isobutylundeca-2,4-dien-8,10-diynamide, and (1R,2S,6R,7R,10S,11R,12R,14S)-10,11-dihydroxy-2,6-dimethyl-12-propan-2-yl-13-oxatetracyclo[8.5.0.02,7.012,14]pentadecane-6-carboxylic acid, all of which are targets of RWLeu4. These compounds are likely to act as inhibitors of the SDR family, which is involved in various metabolic processes, including the detoxification of xenobiotics and the regulation of cellular redox homeostasis. The presence of multiple targets in the SDR family suggests that Norarecoline may exert its effects through a common mechanism, potentially modulating cellular pathways that influence RWLeu4's function. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Norarecoline and RWLeu4, mediated through the SDR family, with the potential for broader implications in disease states involving metabolic dysregulation.",
